# SLURM & cluster conventions

## Dev environment is a Podman container

All cluster work happens inside the `xiaoming-dev` Podman container:

- Start script: `scripts/start-xiaoming-dev-fix-container.sh`
- Image: `docker.io/rocm/primus:v26.2`
- Container mounts `$HOME`, working dir is `~/Primus`
- IPC=host, network=host, exposes `/dev/kfd` `/dev/dri` `/dev/infiniband`

Before running anything on a node, check whether the container already
exists; reuse it. See:

- `.cursor/skills/slurm-xiaoming-dev-container/SKILL.md` — local SLURM
- `.cursor/skills/ssh-node-xiaoming-dev-container/SKILL.md` — SSH then
  enter container

## Picking nodes

- Use `.cursor/skills/slurm-idle-node-check/SKILL.md` to find healthy
  idle nodes (also verifies docker, NIC QoS, RDMA, GIDs).
- Use `.cursor/skills/slurm-training-node-validation/SKILL.md` to
  validate candidate nodes with a real workload before a big job.

## Never

- Do not start long-running training in foreground when on a shared
  login node; always submit via `sbatch`.
- Do not edit other users' jobs.
- Do not commit job scripts that hard-code another user's path; use
  `$HOME` or document the assumption.
